### Implementing LL(1) Parsing
...
[name] @(84, 184) {$note, w=324px, color=emp} **ParseExpr()**
...
[look] @(84, 241) {$note, w=324px} `Peek()` is lookahead.
[choices] @(84, 280) {$table, w=324px, size=24px, pad=12px, colwidths=(45%,55%)} | Token | Production |
|:---|:---|
| num | S → T S′ |
| '(' | S → T S′ |
...
[calls] @(84, 488) {$note, w=324px} Expand the RHS in order:{{br}}first Term,{{br}}then ExprExtra.
% Parser sketches retain the course lexer interface. Error() must not return.
...
[function] @(450, 177) {$code, w=740px, size=27px} ```cpp
void ParseExpr() {
    ParseTerm();
    ParseExprExtra();
}
```
...
!anim function exit
[function2] @(450, 177) {$code, w=740px, size=27px} ```cpp
void ParseExpr() {
  switch (lexer.Peek()) {
    case num:
    case '(':
      ParseTerm();
      ParseExprExtra();
      return;
    default:
      Error();
  }
}
```

