% PowerPoint slides 6.
### Implementing LL(1) Parsing
...
[name] @(84, 184) {$note, w=324px, color=emp} **ParseExprExtra()**
...
[choices] @(84, 280) {$table, w=324px, size=24px, pad=12px, colwidths=(45%,55%)} | Token | Production |
|:---|:---|
| ^ | S′ → ^ S |
| ) or EOF | S′ → ε |
...
[recurse] @(84, 470) {$note, w=324px} After `^`, parse a{{br}}whole Expr. This gives{{br}}{{color=emp|right association}}.
...
[empty] @(84, 607) {$note, w=324px} ε consumes no token.
...
[function] @(450, 171) {$code, w=740px, size=26px} ```cpp
void ParseExprExtra() {
  switch (lexer.Peek()) {
    case '^':
      lexer.Use('^');
      ParseExpr();
      return;
    case ')':
    case EOF:
      return;
    default:
      Error();
  }
}
```
---
% PowerPoint slides 7.
### Implementing LL(1) Parsing
...
[name] @(84, 184) {$note, w=324px, color=emp} **ParseTerm()**
...
[choices] @(84, 280) {$table, w=324px, size=24px, pad=12px, colwidths=(45%,55%)} | Token | Production |
|:---|:---|
| num | T → num |
| ( | T → ( S ) |
...
[paren] @(84, 465) {$note, w=324px} Parentheses contain{{br}}another full expression.
...
[use] @(84, 567) {$note, w=324px, size=25px} `Use(expected)` checks{{br}}and consumes the token.
% Use(expected) is assumed to report an error on a mismatch.
% Normalize source smart quotes and use Error() consistently.
% The top-level driver must also require EOF after parsing the input.
...
[function] @(450, 171) {$code, w=740px, size=25px} ```cpp
void ParseTerm() {
  switch (lexer.Peek()) {
    case num:
      lexer.Use();
      return;
    case '(':
      lexer.Use('(');
      ParseExpr();
      lexer.Use(')');
      return;
    default:
      Error();
  }
}
```

---
### ParseStatement()
% The source slide is code-only; the heading names the function.
[function] @(84, 164) {$code, size=24px} ```cpp
ASTNode ParseStatement() {
  if (lexer.None()) Error("Expected Statement.");

  using namespace emplex;
  switch (lexer.Peek()) {
    case Lexer::ID_VAR:   return ParseStatement_Var();
    case Lexer::ID_IF:    return ParseStatement_If();
    case Lexer::ID_WHILE: return ParseStatement_While();
    case Lexer::ID_PRINT: return ParseStatement_Print();
    case '{':            return ParseStatement_Block();
    // List other statement starts here...
    default:             return ParseStatement_Expression();
  }
}
```
...
[result] @(84, 670) {$note} The selected parser returns an {{color=emp|ASTNode}}.
---
### AST Node Types
{$code, size=24px} ```cpp
enum class ASTType {
  NONE=0,
  BLOCK, IF, WHILE, BREAK, CONTINUE, RETURN,      // Controllers
  CALL, CALL_JS, OP1, OP2, INDEX,                 // Functions
  LIT_CHAR, LIT_DOUBLE, LIT_INT, LIT_STRING, VAR, // Leaves
  UNKNOWN
};
```
---
### An `ASTNode` Structure
{$code, size=24px} ```cpp
class ASTNode {
protected:
  ASTType node_type = ASTType::UNKNOWN;  // Type of this AST node
  Token token;                           // Original token for node
  size_t symbol_id = 0;                  // Unique ID if symbol in table
  std::vector<ASTNode> children{};       // Any sub-trees under this node

  std::string extra_info;                // Extra info for debugging
```
---
### Example Parsing function with `ATSNode` return
{$code, size=24px}```cpp
  [[nodiscard]] ASTNode Parse_Block() {
    Token token = lexer.Use('{');
    symbols.IncScope();
    ASTNode block = ASTNode{ASTType::BLOCK, token};

    while (lexer.Peek() != '}') {
      ASTNode line_node = Parse_Statement();
      block.AddChild( std::move(line_node) );
    }
    lexer.Use('}', "Missing '}' (open on line ", token.line_id, ")");
    symbols.DecScope();

    return block;
  }
```
---
### More complex `Term` parsing...
{$code, size=20px}```cpp
  [[nodiscard]] ASTNode Parse_Term() {
    Token token = lexer.Use();

    switch (token) {
      case '!': case '-':     return ASTNode{ASTType::OP1, token, Parse_Term()};
      case Lexer::ID_LIT_INT: return ASTNode{ASTType::LIT_INT, token};
      case Lexer::ID_ID:      return Parse_ID_Token(token);
      case '(': {
        ASTNode out_node = Parse_Expression();
        lexer.Use(')', "Missing parenthesis");
        return out_node;
        } break;
      default: return TokenError("Unexpected token in Term: ", token);
    }
  }

```
